.TH CHANGELOG 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog \- generate and manage changelogs from fragment files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIcommand options\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBchangelog\fR is a CLI tool for managing project changelogs using structured
fragment files. It provides commands to initialize, create, validate, and generate
release notes from YAML fragment files stored in a project's changelog directory.

The tool follows a fragment-based workflow: developers add small YAML fragments
describing individual changes, then the tool aggregates them into release
changelogs with proper formatting and sorting.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit.

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message for the given command or global options if no command specified.

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase verbosity of output (can be used multiple times).

.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non-essential output messages.
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
The following commands are available:
.TP
\fBinit\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Initialize changelog infrastructure for a new or existing project.

.TP
\fBadd\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Create a new fragment file describing a single change.

.TP
\fBlint\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Validate all fragment files in a directory for correctness and consistency.

.TP
\fBrelease\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Generate release changelog entries from accumulated fragments.

.TP
\fBgenerate\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Regenerate the full changelog from stored fragment data.

.TP
\fBreformat\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Reformat and normalize changelog.yaml or .changes.yaml configuration files.

.TP
\fBcollection\-new\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Initialize a new Ansible collection's changelog directory structure.

.TP
\fBlint\-changelog\-yaml\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Validate the syntax and structure of a changelog.yaml configuration file.

.TP
\fBlog\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Display fragments in a git-log style format with pagination support.

.TP
\fBbump\fR [\fIlevel\fR]
Bump VERSION.txt based on bump label environment variable or CI merge request labels.

.TP
\fBpreview\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Render fragment changes as colored markdown output to stdout.

.TP
\fBlicense\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Print the project license (CYMERTEK Source-Available License).
.SH FILE LOCATIONS
.PP
By default, changelog looks for configuration and fragments in:
.IP \(bu 2
\fIchangelogs/config.yaml\fR \- Project configuration
.IP \(bu 2
\fIchangelogs/fragments/\fR \- Fragment files directory
.IP \(bu 2
\fI.changes.yaml\fR \- Machine-readable change metadata (created on release)
.PP
Use the \fB\-d\fR or \fB\-\-dir\fR flag with individual commands to override these paths.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Initialize a new project:
.nf
    changelog init myproject
.fi

.TP
Add a bugfix fragment:
.nf
    changelog add \\
        --category bugfixes \\
        --issue PG-001 \\
        --text "Fixed crash when processing large files" \\
        --title "Stability improvement"
.fi

.TP
Validate all fragments:
.nf
    changelog lint changelogs/fragments/
.fi

.TP
Generate a release changelog:
.nf
    changelog release --version v1.0.0 --output CHANGELOG.md
.fi

.TP
View fragments in log style:
.nf
    changelog log -d changelogs/fragments/ --page-size 25
.fi
